### 2. "Above-the-Line" Deductions
Even though you are taking the standard deduction, you can still claim "above-the-line" deductions (Adjustments to Income) which lower your Adjusted Gross Income (AGI):

*   **Student Loan Interest:** You paid $3,200, but the IRS caps this deduction at **$2,500**. Additionally, because your Modified Adjusted Gross Income (MAGI) will be roughly $85,000–$90,000, you fall into the 2024 phase-out range for single filers ($80,000–$95,000). This means your maximum $2,500 deduction will be partially reduced based on your exact final income.
