### 3. Handling the Home Office Deduction
Because you have freelance photography income, you can deduct your home office against your self-employment income (it cannot be deducted against your W-2 income). 

*   **Your Home Office Percentage:** 170 sq ft / 720 sq ft = **23.6%**
*   **Actual Expenses Method (Recommended):** You pay $22,560/year in rent ($1,880 x 12). 23.6% of that is **~$5,327**. You can also add 23.6% of your utilities, internet, and renter's insurance to this total.
